<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry IV of Plauen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1510">1510</a>–<a href="/years/1554">1554</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Heinrich IV of Plauen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plauen">Plauen</a> was a member of the Reuss family of Vogtland lords who became Burgrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a> and chancellor of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> under Ferdinand I. As a reward for his loyalty in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-war">Schmalkaldic War</a> he recovered Plauen and other Vogtland lands in 1547, briefly restoring his family's lordship before it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-plauen.jpg" alt="Henry IV of Plauen" width="238" height="132" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Glaser · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HeinrichIVHof.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
